# Backups
Spent a little bit more time looking into this.
The general strategy is
- Pause all containers
- Create an LVM snapshot
- Resume all containers
- Borg backup the snapshot locally (most likely in /home/podman/.borg_cloud)
- Rclone the local borg archive

This will all be run as the podman user, as podman is the runner for the containers.
Will probably have this set as an hourly crontab
I'll probably use borgmatic to handle this.
I'll have both podman and k9 backups use the same drive account
- Backup scripts will run separately under podman and k9 user accounts though for simplicity.

# LVM
Just want a simple role to create the LVM cache and scratch drives in /mnt/nas and /mnt/scratch.
Easiest to hardcode the disk UUIDs for this.
